WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:10.980
76. Prehistoric art. Prehistoric art is art from cultures that did not yet have a

2
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.140
written language. The first pieces of artwork are about 40,000 years old, though experts

3
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:23.420
don't agree on exactly when humans started to make art. The earliest clear works of art

4
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:29.980
come from the Upper Paleolithic era, from 10,000 to 40,000 years ago. Most art from

5
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.980
this era is of three types, stone figurines, cave paintings, and etchings or carvings.

6
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.540
Stone figurines are some of the oldest kinds of art. In fact, the oldest known piece of

7
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:50.660
art is a stone figurine called a Venus figurine. Venus figurines are small stone sculptures

8
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:57.980
of women. This particular sculpture has beautiful round curves but is not very detailed. Several

9
00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:03.540
figurines like this have been found. Almost all of these sculptures have no facial features

10
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.480
but very detailed bodies. Prehistoric cave paintings have been found in several parts

11
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:15.820
of the world. The oldest cave paintings are in Europe, with many in Spain and France.

12
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:22.260
The paintings often show animals, especially buffalo. They also show hunting scenes. Early

13
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:29.940
painters had only five colors to use, white, black, red, brown, and yellow. But with these

14
00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:37.060
colors, they created lasting works of art. Etchings and carvings are also common prehistoric

15
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:44.700
types of art. Prehistoric humans cut pictures into the walls of caves with tools. Like the

16
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:50.140
paintings, these pictures are often of animals or hunts. Some carved deer bones were found

17
00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:56.220
in Korea. They may be up to 40,000 years old, which would make them some of the oldest known

18
00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.380
art in the world. Though the tools prehistoric people had were basic, the art they made still

19
00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:10.300
looks fresh and meaningful. Even 40,000 years ago, human beings wanted to have beauty in their

20
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.140
lives. Perhaps we aren't so different from them.
